      "writtenOn": "2022-11-28T13:40:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, got it! I now can see how this was confusing!\n\nYes, it will increase the size of the DT (i.e. `self.header.totalsize`) but `self.bytes` is a slice representing the buffer containing the DT, which might be larger than the DT itself (and needs to be if we\u0027re going to extend it, as you noted). When we `unpack` the DT, we let libfdt know the size of the buffer itself (`fdt_open_into` [sets `totalsize` to the buffer size](https://android.git.corp.google.com/platform/external/dtc/+/refs/heads/master/libfdt/fdt_rw.c#479)) so it can assess how much extra space it has for adding new nodes or properties.\n\nAs a result, I\u0027m renaming `self.bytes` as `self.buffer` in aosp/2319816.",
      "parentUuid": "15ae4f4e_07eae353",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 553,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 557,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "bc94b73e10b43bb9e33cfab5d0da211f18509151",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
