      "writtenOn": "2022-11-25T21:19:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Though why does failing to apply an overlay result in a corrupt FDT?\n\nBecause `fdt_overlay_apply` doesn\u0027t patch the DT atomically so can leave it in an intermediate state. As it patches phandles sequentially, I suppose that running `overlay_fixup_phandle` on only half of a DT would break phandles references between its halves.\n\n\u003e The caller still has the `\u0026mut Fdt` that it passed in, which I guess is now corrupt.\n\nYou\u0027re right! That\u0027s not really an issue with this implementation as the caller then `?` the result, causing the reference to go out of scope, but this still feels fragile.\n\nAny idea on how to address it? Make `apply_debug_policy` unsafe for the same reason? intentionally",
      "parentUuid": "6ce9e61e_b4d06b1c",
      "revId": "bc94b73e10b43bb9e33cfab5d0da211f18509151",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
